WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
The Islamic calendar does not
count from the Prophet's birth.

2
00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.090
It starts in 622.

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.680
That year, Muhammad and
his followers left Makkah.

4
00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.040
Muslims believe his enemies
had plotted to kill him.

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.400
Under cover of night, they travelled
about 450 kilometres north,

6
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.860
to a new home.

7
00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:22.630
Muslims call this journey
the Hijrah: the migration.

8
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.650
So why count the years from an
escape, and not from a birth?

9
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.610
In this mission, you'll
follow his life in Makkah:

10
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:34.750
an orphan, a trader, then,
Muslims believe, God's messenger.

11
00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.660
Then you'll read the first words
Muslims believe God revealed to him,

12
00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.590
and weigh up why the
journey still matters.

13
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:45.710
Your mission: find out what
made one escape so important.
